  "construction_notes": [
    {
      "text": "Parcel match: state APNs 019-042-150, -160, -170 aren't in the county layer. 019-042-190 is the only other non-house parcel in that assessor block, beside 880 Glenview, 2.56 acres against 3.28 stated, with no address or owner shown. Matched by block only.",
      "src": [
        "SRC-001910"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "HCD APR lists the project as Highland Ridge (2024 entitlement row, 850 Glenview Dr, APNs 019-042-150, -160, -170, 58 units approved 2024-05-21) and Glenview Highlands (2023 application row). The developer markets it as The Highlands at 800 Glenview Dr. The 2022 APR shows the earlier Glenview Terrace approval on the same APNs: 29 single-family units (1 low, 3 moderate, 25 above moderate), entitled 2022-07-01.",
      "src": [
        "SRC-001123",
        "SRC-001129",
        "SRC-003418"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "ALUC application: site is a parking lot, vacant church and vacant house on 3.28 acres; nine three-story buildings (A through I), 41 ft tall. Developer page: Plan 1 1,450 sf from $1,249,990; Plan 3 1,480 sf from $1,419,990; Plan 2 1,760 sf from $1,449,990; all three-story with two-car garages, owned solar.",
      "src": [
        "SRC-003419",
        "SRC-003418"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "2025 APR building permit rows cover Buildings C (6 units, incl. 1 low-income, issued 2025-06-06) and G (5 units, incl. 1 moderate-income, issued 2025-06-30) only.",
      "src": [
        "SRC-001123"
      ]
    }
